==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|scarcely}}, {{m|enm|scarsly}}, {{m|enm|scarsely}}, {{m|enm|scarsliche}}, {{m|enm|scarseliche}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|scarce|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈskɛəsli/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈskɛɹsli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-scarcely.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|scarce|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|modal}} [[probably|Probably]] not.
#: {{ux|en|One could '''scarcely''' find any trout in the stream without the stocking program.}}
# {{lb|en|modal}} [[certainly|Certainly]] not.
#: {{ux|en|One could '''scarcely''' expect the man to know how to fly a helicopter.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1842|author={{w|William Godwin}}|title=An Enquiry Concerning Political Justice|passage=He did not enter upon the subject without being aware that government by its very nature counteracts the improvement of individual intellect; but, as the views he entertains in this particular are out of the common road, it is '''scarcely''' to be wondered at that he understood the proposition more completely as he proceeded, and saw more distinctly into the nature of the remedy.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1869|author={{w|R. D. Blackmore}}|title=[[s:Lorna Doone/Chapter 45|Lorna Doone]]|passage=But, of course, this weather had put a stop to every kind of movement; for even if men could have borne the cold, they could '''scarcely''' be brought to face the perils of the snow-drifts.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1898|author={{w|H. G. Wells}}|title=[[s:The War of the Worlds/Book 1/Chapter 1|The War of the Worlds]]|passage=The planet Mars, I '''scarcely''' need remind the reader, revolves about the sun at a mean distance of 140,000,000 miles, and the light and heat it receives from the sun is barely half of that received by this world.}}
#* '''1914''', {{w|Saki}}, ''[[s:Dusk|Dusk]]'' in ''[[w:Beasts and Super-Beasts|Beasts and Super-Beasts]]'',
#*: His clothes could '''scarcely''' be called shabby, at least they passed muster in the half-light, but one’s imagination could not have pictured the wearer embarking on the purchase of a half-crown box of chocolates or laying out ninepence on a carnation buttonhole.
# {{lb|en|degree}} Hardly: only just; by a small margin.
#* {{RQ:Irving Tales of a Traveller|passage=He had '''scarcely''' finished, when the labourer arrived who had been sent for my ransom.}}
#* '''1875''' December 7, {{w|Ulysses S. Grant}}, ''[[s:Ulysses S. Grant's Seventh State of the Union Address|Ulysses S. Grant's Seventh State of the Union Address]]'',
#*: In 1776 manufactories '''scarcely''' existed even in name in all this vast territory.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1887|author={{w|Arthur Conan Doyle}}|title={{w|A Study in Scarlet}}|passage='''Scarcely''' had she got fairly into it, however, before the beasts closed in behind her, and she found herself completely embedded in the moving stream of fierce-eyed long-homed bullocks.<!--use for time-->}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1905|author=[[w:Emma Orczy|Baroness Emmuska Orczy]]| title=[[w:The Case of Miss Elliott|The Disappearance of Count Collini]]| chapter=2| url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL8479084W| passage=&ldquo;'''Scarcely''' had Alice reached her twentieth birthday, than she gave her erstwhile fiancée [sic] his formal congé.&nbsp;[…]”}}
#* {{RQ:Williams Velveteen Rabbit|passage=That night, and for many nights after, the Velveteen Rabbit slept in the Boy’s bed. At first he found it rather uncomfortable, for the Boy hugged him very tight, and sometimes he rolled over on him, and sometimes he pushed him so far under the pillow that the Rabbit could '''scarcely''' breathe.}}
#* '''1963''', {{w|Pierre Boulle}}, {{w|Planet of the Apes (novel)|''Planet of the Apes''}}:
#*: But we shall take '''scarcely''' more than two years to reach it, while we should have needed almost as much time to arrive in the region of Proxima Centauris.<!--use before a comparative-->
#* '''1993''', {{w|Baltasar Gracián}}, Joseph Jacobs (translator), ''The Art of Worldly Wisdom'',
#*: Nature '''scarcely''' ever gives us the very best—for that we must have recourse to art.

====Usage notes====
It is grammatically a negative word. It therefore collocates with ''[[ever]]'' rather than ''[[never]]''.
* Compare ''We '''scarcely''' ever eat fish.'' with ''We almost never eat fish.''
* The sentence ''We '''scarcely''' never eat fish'' is ungrammatical.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|degree: by a small margin}} {{l|en|barely}}, {{l|en|hardly}}
* {{sense|barely, almost not or not quite}} {{l|en|barely}}, {{l|en|just}}, {{l|en|hardly}}, {{l|en|only just}}

